  "design": {
    "decision": "Every round, hold a top [♠] or a guarded winner back for trick 13 instead of spending it to make the contract sooner. Buying early pays more, so it also changes when in the run to take it.",
    "opponent": "Revealed the first time it grows. Opponents then fight for trick 13 by saving their own top trump, or by drawing trumps early.",
    "rationale": "The brief asks for Streaks pieces built on the last trick, and there is no kept uncommon last-trick payoff. Every uncommon variant was cut for stacked contract scaling or a narrow card filter. Growth makes trick 13 a recurring stake across the run, which a flat per-round payout cannot. Growth pieces have measured weak, so the step starts high, with the last trick firing about 48% of rounds. This is the sigil's one condition and one effect.",
